Original commit body from 02ab5e6:

Two changes work together to fix commit body loss during squash merge:

1. Add SQUASH_TEMPLATE.md with ${PullRequestTitle} and ${PullRequestDescription}
   placeholders. Forgejo uses this template when performing squash merges,
   including the full PR description in the final commit message.

2. Fix auto-pr script to preserve newlines in commit descriptions:
   - Remove `tr '\n' ' ' | sed` pipeline that collapsed body to single line
   - Remove explicit newline stripping in do_pr()
   - Remove newline stripping in flush_queue()
   - Properly escape newlines (\n) when storing in JSON queue file

Before: Squash commits had only subject + trailers (~118 chars)
After: Squash commits include full PR description with formatting

This restores the detailed commit history that was lost when we switched
from merge to squash in commit 8f6c03de.
